{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"f0257da221e794548c706b2cbc2caac8dd764d8e9c63fc1d5e1db21b766a43b9","packTokens":2693,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":208,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":999,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1380,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using authorized Folio3 Google accounts and have employee and vehicle profiles populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking and schedule releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can receive notifications and claim available spaces first-come, first-served.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record verification attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and automatically email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Who receives a push notification when a space becomes available, and what should happen if delivery fails or a recipient has notifications disabled?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Notify all eligible employees without dedicated parking; availability remains claimable in the app even if a push notification is not delivered.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What exact actions may Parking Administrators perform, especially when a holder's release has already been claimed and requires administrator intervention?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Manage employee and parking records, configuration, and reports; also reverse a claimed release when needed, recording the intervention.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"What application access, if any, does a Security Guard need for entrance verification and recording entry status?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Provide a guard-facing view of verification results and a way to record whether the vehicle entered.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Can an employee without dedicated parking claim more than one temporary space for the same date, and can they cancel or relinquish a claim before entry?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allow at most one claim per employee per date, with no user cancellation after a successful claim.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How should daily/weekly utilization and the overall utilization percentage be calculated, including the denominator and the treatment of released but unclaimed spaces?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Define utilization as occupied spaces divided by total available spaces for each reporting period; report released and claimed totals separately and exclude released-but-unclaimed spaces from occupied counts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"May employees add, update, or deactivate their registered vehicle details after first-time setup, or must changes be made by an administrator?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Employees can manage their own vehicle records; administrators can also manage them.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"When a claimant has multiple registered vehicles, which plate should be authorized for that temporary parking claim?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require the employee to select one registered vehicle when claiming; authorize only that plate for the claim.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How will entry events for stickered dedicated vehicles be captured for utilization, given that those vehicles bypass system verification?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Have the LPR system record their plate-entry events without requiring authorization verification.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the 32 requirements be approved as one run despite the estimate of about three runs’ worth of work, or should the one-run scope be reduced?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 32 requirements as one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"When a Parking Administrator reverses a claimed release, should the claimant’s temporary parking authorization for that date be revoked immediately, or should the reversal be recorded without revoking that authorization?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allow the administrator to reverse the claimed release and record the intervention, without automatically revoking the claimant’s temporary parking authorization.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Require successful Google authentication with a verified corporate email matching an active directory employee before granting an employee session; refresh employee profiles and parking assignments from current source records, and deny dashboard access with retry or support guidance if the profile cannot be retrieved.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Populate refreshed dedicated-employee profiles with employee ID and name, dedicated-parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle details; require non-dedicated employees without a registered plate to register one before vehicle-dependent parking actions, showing a registration screen on first login and a prompt on a returning employee’s dashboard.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Allow employees to add, update, or deactivate only their own vehicle records, and allow Parking Administrators to manage employee vehicle records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Treat assigned dedicated parking as reserved on operating days unless released; let holders release today’s space with one home-screen action, view its current status, and schedule releases for operating dates within the next 30 calendar dates in the office’s local timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Make scheduled releases claimable at the configured daily release time, and make today’s release claimable at that time if released earlier or immediately if released at or after that time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Let holders cancel unclaimed releases; require administrator intervention to reverse claimed releases, record the intervention, and preserve the claimant’s temporary parking authorization.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Notify every eligible non-dedicated employee with push notifications enabled when spaces become available, while keeping available spaces claimable in the application if notification delivery fails or is disabled.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Allocate each released space to the first successfully committed eligible claim, reject competing claims and duplicate claims by the same employee for a date, and return the current claimable-space count to non-dedicated employees and display it in the application.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Require an employee claiming a temporary space to select one registered vehicle and authorize only that vehicle’s plate; assign and return a parking floor for each successful claim, and do not allow employees to cancel or relinquish successful claims.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Parking Administrators to manage employee and parking records, operating-day calendars, release-time settings, report settings, and stakeholder email addresses; restrict administrative employee, parking, configuration, and report-management actions to authenticated Parking Administrators.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Ignore pedestrians, motorcycles, and other non-car objects reported by entrance LPR, and record plate-entry events for vehicles with permanent Folio3 parking stickers without temporary-authorization verification.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"For non-stickered vehicles, normalize plate case and permitted spacing, require an exact match to a current-day temporary authorization, and activate the green indicator only for a match.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Fail closed when a plate is unreadable or the camera, indicator, connection, or authorization service is unavailable; keep the green indicator inactive, alert security for a service failure, and record the failure when service is restored.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Record each entrance verification attempt with its timestamp, plate when available, verification result, and entry status; permit only authenticated Security Guards to view verification results and record vehicle entry status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"At reporting-period close, record unused dedicated parking when the holder neither released nor used the space, and unused temporary parking when the claimant’s registered vehicle did not enter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Calculate utilization as occupied spaces divided by total available spaces, report released and claimed totals separately, exclude released-but-unclaimed spaces from occupied counts, and provide daily and weekly values with the total available-space denominator.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"At the configured Monday report time in the office’s local timezone, generate and email the weekly utilization report to configured stakeholders, including unused-parking records, daily and weekly utilization, released totals, temporary-claim totals, and utilization percentage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Provide Parking Administrators with on-screen parking reports, filters, and CSV export, and do not apply automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on utilization records.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}